Package: vitalBayes
Title: Bayesian Vital Rate Estimation for Elasmobranchs
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: 
    person(given = c("Brian", "J"), family = "Moe", email = "brian.moe@MYFWC.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A comprehensive framework for estimating population vital rates in 
    elasmobranch fishes using Bayesian hierarchical models. The package implements 
    an integrated four-stage workflow: birth size estimation, maturity ogives 
    (length and age at 50% maturity), individual growth curves (von Bertalanffy, 
    Gompertz, Logistic), and natural mortality with survival simulation. Key 
    features include partial pooling for imbalanced sex ratios, maturity-based 
    growth parameterization that derives k from observable milestones, joint 
    posterior sampling for mortality estimation preserving parameter correlations, 
    and CV-based prior specification. Implements Chen-Watanabe, Peterson-Wroblewski, 
    and Lorenzen mortality models with Monte Carlo uncertainty propagation. All 
    models are fit via Stan using precompiled models for fast, reproducible inference.
